The proposed solution makes a small oversight by assuming $y > 0$ ("By symmetry, take $y>0$"). Since a lattice point simply requires integer coordinates, $y = 0$ is also valid, corresponding to the point $(36, 0)$ on the line $x = 36$. 

When $y = 0$, the distance from the origin is $d = 36$ (which corresponds to the factor pair $a=18, b=18$ for $ab = 324$). Including this missing distance gives $829 + 36 = 865$.

